Z||000036||william_thorniii||12-17-1999||06:03 PM||||Monkey,<P>I thought that my statement that "U-haul claims that a Fiero can't be towed with a dolly" was enough (wink-wink) of a hint (wink-wink) that we are all really small Pontiac (wink-wink) owners.  If they ask you what kind.. just say small two door Pontiac from the 80's (wink-wink).  The usual response on their part is "Is it a Grand Am?" Then that jogs your memory (wink-wink) and you proclaim "Why yes, I believe that it might (wink-wink) be a Grand Am"  <P>****DISCLAIMER**** Please note, that I am in no way condoning or encourageing blasphemy.  What you all engage in on your own time though.. (wink-wink)<P>Now do you get it? <P>William T. Thorn, III (wink-wink)||||reg||1
Z||000037||batboy||12-17-1999||09:12 PM||||I bought my flatbed car hauling trailer for about $1600 brand new. As much as it's been used, it's almost paid for itself. It's a 18 footer (including the 2 foot dovetail) tandem axle with electric brakes. I paid a small amount extra for the 6 foot ramps rather than the standard 5 foot ramps. With the dovetail (the back part of the trailer slants down a little) and the longer ramps, I have no problem running Fieros up onto it.||||reg||1
